 "description": "Decide whether a captured 402 challenge can actually be paid. Separates defects that stop a payment being constructed from ones that merely make the call harder to get right, and checks the resource is bound to the endpoint that served it - a challenge naming a different resource would, if paid, satisfy a requirement for something else. Also names the price spread when several payments are accepted. Nothing is fetched and nothing is paid. Pay 100000 atomic USDC on Base via exact x402. MCP does not pay; it provides a challenge handoff.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "challenge": {
    "description": "A 402 challenge you already captured: the raw body as JSON, or a base64 payment-required header. Nothing is fetched, so this works against any endpoint including one behind authentication or on a private network.",
